---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { KOFI_URL, REPO_URL } from '../../config.js';
---
<Legal locale="en" route="imprint" title="Imprint" description="Provider identification and contact for the Nemo website.">
  <p class="placeholder">Placeholder: this page is not filled in yet. The operator adds the details below; this is not legal advice.</p>

  <h2>Information according to § 5 DDG (German Digital Services Act)</h2>
  <p>
    [PLACEHOLDER: first and last name]<br />
    [PLACEHOLDER: street and number]<br />
    [PLACEHOLDER: postcode and city]<br />
    [PLACEHOLDER: country]
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    E-mail: [PLACEHOLDER: e-mail address]<br />
    [PLACEHOLDER, optional: phone number]
  </p>

  <h2>Responsible for the content</h2>
  <p>[PLACEHOLDER: name and address as above, if different]</p>

  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This website is a private, non-commercial project. The Nemo app is open source (MIT licence) and free; source code on <a href={REPO_URL} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.</li>
    <li>Voluntary support goes through <a href={KOFI_URL} rel="noopener">Ko-fi</a>, an external provider. Payments are handled only there.</li>
    <li>The website sets no cookies and embeds no third-party content. It is served by Cloudflare Pages (see the <a href="/en/privacy">privacy policy</a>).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What usually belongs here in Germany</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    For orientation, not legal advice: the provider’s name and a postal address, an e-mail address for quick contact, for editorial content the person responsible;
    for businesses additionally the legal form, representatives, register and VAT ID. For a private, free website, name, address and e-mail are usually enough.
    Whether an imprint is required depends on the individual case.
  </p>
</Legal>
